From 7ddd22ef666ac10b572ddfe7a9e53cf5082697c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Sen=C3=A9n=20de=20Diego?= <senendds@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Mar 2026 00:45:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Use local .strm files as subtitle anchors

Use the local .strm path to find, save and browse associated subtitles
instead of the resolved playback URL. Resolved plugin routes ending in .strm
continue to use their dynamic path because they do not represent local files.

Preserve library labels when playback-state updates resolve a .strm item to a
remote resource, and redact paths from the new diagnostic logs.
